[# docs-src/repos/cx-tooling.cxd — the editor and diagram surface's page,
   repo-cx-tooling.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 4). Facts
   from the registries; the one example from its own corpus (the diagram
   suite). #]

[repo name=cx-tooling
  [intro
    """The editor knows the language because the language tells
       it. `cx-tooling` is the editor and diagram surface: the VS Code
       extension, the Neovim and Helix configuration, the tree-sitter
       grammar, the shell completions, the TextMate syntax, the installer
       scripts, the Linguist submission, the `<cx-diagram>` web component and
       the repository template every component repository starts from — plus
       the CX half of `cx-stdlib/diagram`, the one bundled module that left
       the frozen standard library for the product that consumes it."""]
  [body
    """Three layers stack on the `cx` binary — a TextMate grammar for display
       contexts, the language server for live editing, tree-sitter for
       structure and injection — and the front door holds them to the
       binary: the completions are checked against the CLI's own subcommand
       and flag catalog, the grammars and the parity register against the
       lexer and the language server, each a step of the front door that
       reads this repository from its pin. A verb added to `cx` without its
       completion is a failed step, not a stale editor. [[editors]] and [[cli]]
       are the guide's pages."""]
  [body
    """The diagram renderer is a pure CX program: it renders a program's
       image to Mermaid carrying the source as round-trip metadata, emits
       DOT, splices the source into SVG and PNG, and recovers it from all
       three; its rules table is a sealed value the completeness gate diffs
       against the spec, the golden corpus and the grammar registry. Its V
       half — the C ABI export, the goldens — stays with the language core,
       so `diagram` is a two-repository module, like the others that
       straddle a boundary ([[cli-diagram]] is the command surface)."""]
  [gives
    """One module of the standard library — pure, Ring 1 — bundled into the
       build from the pin, its specification and corpus travelling with it;
       it links to the reference page projected from its own documentation.
       The editor surface ships as files, not a module: install it with the
       scripts under `tooling/install/`."""]
  [try
    """Render a one-node program to Mermaid and read the source back out of
       the rendering: the round trip is the contract — a diagram is a
       projection of the program, never a drawing beside it."""]
  [fixture id=diagram-001-render-mermaid]
  [status
    """The tooling repository ships as an editor surface: its module is
       bundled into the build from the pin, and the front door's editor
       checks read the completions, grammars and parity register from the
       same checkout, so what the editor knows and what the binary does are
       graded together."""]]
